 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 17368, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XfgmeFu5Uvk8FMs8j97S3d", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19997, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Srw12bSZcipopn6ryJoFit", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production. Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.2.9 and v2.3.0 were both healthy before v2.3.1). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the regions mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed in all three regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west, eu-west; healthy=true; error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback attempt; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until fixed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2024-incident-1"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 50597, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Srw12bSZcipopn6ryJoFit", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2024-incident-1", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 50597, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Srw12bSZcipopn6ryJoFit", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 51703, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Tiu47Pc5bHrSg9mneVyjPZ", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 52003, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Tiu47Pc5bHrSg9mneVyjPZ", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 52003, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Tiu47Pc5bHrSg9mneVyjPZ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 53921, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.002).\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy. v2.3.1 is the unhealthy one, so no change-manager approval was needed. The first attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the regions split between v2.3.0 and v2.3.1. I retried the same rollback, and it completed in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Incident:** The SEV2 incident creation timed out, but when I checked, incident INC-0001 already existed with the full description. I did not create a duplicate. It records the failure, the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the current state.\n\nFollow-ups for the team: investigate why v2.3.1 fails health checks, and look into the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it is fixed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01SFhFDawxUFT1DxzqHC4Ph1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01HtXbhrVD6SMVt3GprHmUMW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "chec